# Copy to .env and fill in ONE of the two blocks below. `.env` itself is gitignored, and a
# `.env` at the repository root works too — all the live suites read it.
#
# The run fails if neither block is complete. There is no skip path: a gateway suite that
# quietly runs zero tests is worse than one that tells you it is not configured.

# --- Option 1: let the suite provision its own gateway (this is how CI runs) ---
# An org-scoped API key for a THROWAWAY org. The suite creates a project there, mints a
# credential scoped to `ai_gateway:invoke`, and deletes both when the run ends. It also
# sweeps stale `neon-ts-e2e-*` projects on start, so never point this at an org holding
# anything worth keeping. Model access is granted per account, so the org needs access to
# every model in MATRIX_MODELS (see e2e/helpers.ts).
NEON_API_KEY=
NEON_ORG_ID=

# --- Option 2: run against a branch you already have ---
# Fill both or neither. `neon env pull` on a branch whose neon.ts enables `preview.aiGateway`
# writes exactly these two. Leave them empty otherwise: a placeholder that looks like a real
# token is worse than no value at all.
NEON_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=
NEON_AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
